    <bpmn:task id="task_1mv0e90e" name="Fix wingtip z-fighting" dai:notes="Flicker on the wing edges in the hangar was z-fighting, not depth precision (24-bit depth, near 0.5 m, camera 14 m away). Confirmed by recolouring faces in the live mesh: the wingtip caps ended flush with the wing, so their end faces shared a plane (biplane x = ±4.3, turboprop ±4.9). New tests/mesh.test.ts finds every pair of overlapping, coplanar (within 4 mm), same-facing, differently coloured faces across all styles, wheels and stripe paints. It also found: paint stripes ending flush with the fuselage block, elevators as wide as the tailplanes, and the jet stripe flush with its accent band. Fixes in planeMesh.ts: caps are larger and stick 3 cm past the wing tip, stripes 10 cm shorter (jet stripe wider than the band), elevators 10 cm narrower. Tests 43/43; checked with canvas captures at several turntable angles." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_abwugsv3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_elpyus10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_abwugsv3" sourceRef="task_pjdrvauj" targetRef="task_1mv0e90e" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_w52k1d09" name="Fix runway marking z-fighting" dai:notes="Runway paint (threshold keys, numbers, centreline, touchdown bars) sat 4 cm above the asphalt in the same mesh, which z-fought at approach distances (24-bit depth resolves only a few cm at 1 km). Raised the markings to 10 cm above the asphalt (top 0.31 m) and moved them into their own mesh with a separate material (polygonOffset factor -4, units -16 vs the strip&#39;s -2/-4), created once per world and disposed with it. Checked with zoomed canvas captures on a 3° approach at 400 m, 1.2 km and 2 km: markings solid, no flicker. Tests 43/43." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_elpyus10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_8sjdjlm2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_elpyus10" sourceRef="task_1mv0e90e" targetRef="task_w52k1d09" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_miq54ef9" name="Landing 15% more forgiving" dai:notes="flight.ts: LANDING_FORGIVENESS = 1.15 scales all touchdown crash limits (nose-in, cartwheel wing strike, tail strike, prop nose-over); REBOUND_DAMPING = 2 makes the strut damp extension twice as hard as compression; DEFAULT_SPEC.gearC 6000 → 6900. game.ts: landing grade sink thresholds (A &#60; 1.72, B &#60; 3.45 m/s with medium tyres) and bank (&#60; 6°) ×1.15. hud.ts: sink warning turns red above 3.45 m/s. Measured with a headless drop test: the crash limit was already high (≈11 m/s level), so the main difficulty was bouncing; biplane bounce height at 2/3/4 m/s sink went 0.19/1.27/0.88 m → 0.15/0.92/0.56 m (≈30% lower); tricycle planes did not bounce in the test. Tests 43/43 incl. the every-loadout landing matrix. Not hand-flown yet." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_8sjdjlm2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_oifen32e</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_8sjdjlm2" sourceRef="task_w52k1d09" targetRef="task_miq54ef9" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_ta8rbc88" name="Main menu flyover + separate hangar screen" dai:notes="The app opens on the main menu over the terrain flyover again (orbit of the home airfield). The menu shows the current aircraft and a Hangar button (H, gamepad Y). New &#39;hangar&#39; game state and #hangar-screen: plane turntable in front of the hangar + customization panel + &#39;Back to menu&#39; (Esc / Enter / Backspace / gamepad B). FLY! only on the main menu. Preview is built when entering the hangar and disposed when leaving; camera FOV reset to 70 on return. Pause and debrief buttons renamed &#39;Main menu&#39;. README controls updated. Checked in Chrome: load → menu (camera 677 m from the field), Hangar → preview, ↓ changes plane, Esc → menu with updated aircraft line, H reopens, Fly from menu starts the sortie with the chosen plane, back to menu has no preview; no errors. Tests 43/43." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_oifen32e</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_0jnu5ncg</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_oifen32e" sourceRef="task_miq54ef9" targetRef="task_ta8rbc88" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_cvbxb9rh" name="Low clouds you can fly through" dai:notes="clouds.ts: cloud base is now 200-460 m above the terrain under the cloud (was 760-1240 m above sea level); each puff is also kept ≥ 120 m above the ground below it. Measured on one seed: puff undersides min 106 m, p10 214 m, median 313 m AGL. game.ts: whiteout is a smoothed value: up to fully white at 6/s when the camera is in a cloud (≈0.2 s), back to clear at 0.7/s after leaving (≈1.4 s); only during a sortie; held while paused. index.html: #whiteout moved under the HUD canvas so instruments stay readable in cloud. Menu flyover lowered from 170 to 110 m so it stays under the cloud base. Checked in Chrome by flying a plane straight through a puff: 0 → 1.0 in 0.2 s, 1.0 while inside, then a smooth 1.4 s fade to 0; captures show low clouds around the airfield and a full white-out inside. Tests 43/43." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_0jnu5ncg</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_frb4zovq</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_0jnu5ncg" sourceRef="task_ta8rbc88" targetRef="task_cvbxb9rh" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_j24gc04j" name="Hangar: plane left, dialog right" dai:notes="game.ts updatePreview: the camera&#39;s view offset (setViewOffset) slides the image so the plane sits in the middle of the free space left of the hangar dialog: shift = W/2 − panelLeft/2, eased in, recomputed every frame so it follows window resizes; no shift when the dialog drops below the view on narrow screens. Cleared on leaving the hangar. Checked in Chrome at 1440 px: dialog 982-1382 px, plane centre at 491 px = free-space centre, for the Jet and the Biplane; main menu has no offset afterwards. Tests 43/43." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_frb4zovq</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_vh53qzhx</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_frb4zovq" sourceRef="task_cvbxb9rh" targetRef="task_j24gc04j" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_zlhj5tfe" name="Fix blocked cockpit view" dai:notes="Cause: the cockpit camera sat inside (turboprop, jet) or on the edge of (biplane) the pilot&#39;s head, and inside the turboprop/jet canopy; the ink-outline hull (back faces) of those parts surrounded the camera, and the near plane (0.5 m) cut the fuselage just below the eye, exposing its outline hull as a black band. Fix: planeMesh.ts builds the pilot (head, goggles, scarf), canopy and biplane windscreen as a separate &#39;cockpit&#39; mesh; setCockpitView(on) hides it and the plane&#39;s own outline meshes. game.ts sets it every frame from the camera mode (not during the crash orbit) and moves the eye points to biplane (0,1.05,0.05), turboprop (0,1.02,-0.6), jet (0,0.95,-2.36) so the fuselage stays beyond the near plane. Checked in Chrome with canvas captures on the runway and in the air for all three planes: clear forward view (biplane between the struts under the top wing, turboprop and jet over the nose); chase view restores pilot and outlines. Tests 43/43." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_vh53qzhx</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_ctr5squx</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_vh53qzhx" sourceRef="task_j24gc04j" targetRef="task_zlhj5tfe" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_90h01vcy" name="Cockpit dashboard covers the lower view" dai:notes="planeMesh.ts buildDash(): a cockpit instrument panel shown only in cockpit view, placed from the airframe eye point (moved from game.ts into AIRFRAMES[].eye): 3.6 m wide (covers 21:9), 0.8 m ahead, top edge ~20° below eye level, tilted toward the pilot, with a rim in the paint colour and three gauges; the middle needle follows engine RPM. It draws after the scene (renderOrder 10) with depthFunc ALWAYS, so the fuselage between the eye and the panel cannot cover it, while it still writes depth (depthTest = false would stop depth writes in WebGL, letting water and ink edges bleed through: seen and fixed). Checked with canvas captures in the air for all three planes: no landscape below the dashboard edge or in the lower corners; horizon, nose and runway ahead visible. Tests 43/43." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_ctr5squx</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_lrgd2601</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_ctr5squx" sourceRef="task_zlhj5tfe" targetRef="task_90h01vcy" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_ninoqfv1" name="&#34;Built with DAI Studio&#34; badge" dai:notes="index.html + style.css: a pill-shaped link &#34;Built with DAI Studio&#34; (dark navy #121826, grey text, bold purple #7b61e8 &#34;DAI Studio&#34;, hover border) fixed in the top-right corner of every screen, including in flight; opens https://dai.studio in a new tab; smaller on screens under 560 px. hud.ts: the in-flight minimap moved from y 12 to y 62 so it sits below the badge. Checked in Chrome: badge at 1236,16 (188×36) on menu, hangar (no overlap with the dialog), pause and in flight; HUD canvas is empty under the badge and the minimap starts below it. Tests 43/43." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_lrgd2601</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_a8shfvpr</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_lrgd2601" sourceRef="task_90h01vcy" targetRef="task_ninoqfv1" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_pi4xelr0" name="Smaller DAI Studio badge" dai:notes="Badge shrunk from 188×36 to 147×26 px (12 px text, 5×12 px padding, 12 px from the corner; 11 px text on phones). Minimap moved up to y 46 to stay just below it. Checked in Chrome: badge 1281,12 147×26; HUD empty under it, minimap starts below." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_a8shfvpr</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_lab9ajwq</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
