    <bpmn:task id="task_d7qgj71h" name="Flaps" dai:notes="flight.ts: ControlInput.flaps (lever 0..1), PlaneState.flaps (position) and flapsBlown; FLAP_NOTCHES [0, 0.5, 1] = UP / T/O / LAND. PlaneSpec: flapCl 0.6 (extra CL at full flap), flapCd 0.07 × deflection², flapStall 0.02 rad (stalls a little earlier), flapTrim 0.03 rad (trimmed AoA drops, less ballooning), flapRate 0.6/s, flapSpeed (biplane 30, turboprop 52, jet 65 m/s ≈ 1.6× clean stall). Above flapSpeed the allowed deflection falls to 0 at 1.3× (blow-back, quicker than the motor). liftCoefficient / stallAlphaAt / stallSpeed take the flap position; the stall warning and the Arcade stall protection use it. composeSpec(default) is still DEFAULT_SPEC. input.ts: flap lever notch, stepFlaps(); game.ts: F / V and gamepad d-pad ↓ / ↑ in flight, toast &#39;FLAPS T/O&#39;, lever reset each sortie, take-off hint mentions F, one-time &#39;full flaps&#39; tip when descending below 350 m within 2.5 km of a field (the destination in Cross-country). planeMesh.ts: flapL / flapR hinged surfaces on the inner trailing edge (biplane lower wing, turboprop low wing, jet swept wing inboard of the ailerons), up to 35° down. hud.ts: gauge panel 150 → 182 px with a FLAPS row (three notch boxes, lever highlighted, a pointer for the real position, red &#39;FLAPS — TOO FAST!&#39;). Headless (medium wheels), clean → T/O take-off, full-flap landing: biplane run 92→78 m, touchdown 89→66 km/h, roll 151→63 m; turboprop 236→197 m, 156→122 km/h, 336→224 m; jet 311→256 m, 185→148 km/h, 469→334 m. Tests 61/61: lift/stall numbers, travel, blow-back, full-flap glide ~44% steeper (averaged; a single instant was noisy from the phugoid), and all 9 flight loadouts take off shorter and land slower with flaps. README and in-game controls updated; tsc and build OK. NOT verified in the browser (the Chrome extension was not connected): the flap surfaces, HUD row and toasts." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_a4ql207j</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_q1khgvd1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_a4ql207j" sourceRef="task_4ihayk5l" targetRef="task_d7qgj71h" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_lr8p0ppi" name="Brakes +10% bite" dai:notes="Brake friction ×1.1 for every tyre: hard 0.55 → 0.605, medium 0.45 → 0.495, soft 0.38 → 0.418; DEFAULT_SPEC.brakeFriction 0.45 → 0.495 so the default loadout still equals the base spec. Headless clean landing rolls (test pilot brakes 0.6 s after touchdown), before → after: biplane 142/151/160 → 138/148/157 m (hard/medium/soft), turboprop 291/336/423 → 273/314/394 m, jet 403/469/599 → 375/437/556 m. The biplane changes least because most of its short roll happens before the brakes go on. No nose-overs: all 9 flight loadouts land and stop, with and without flaps. Tests 61/61, tsc OK." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_q1khgvd1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_8tj5iymd</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_q1khgvd1" sourceRef="task_d7qgj71h" targetRef="task_lr8p0ppi" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_yg0oghzt" name="Clearer FLAPS row on the HUD" dai:notes="hud.ts: gauge panel 182 → 218 px. A dashed divider at y 156 separates the throttle / rpm line (y 142) from the flaps; the FLAPS label moved from y 152 to 176. Next to it &#39;(V ↔ F)&#39; in the muted brown; the notch row runs UP → T/O → LAND left to right, so V moves the lever left (less flap) and F right (more). When blown back the label and the selected notch turn red and the hint reads &#39;TOO FAST — slow down!&#39; while the position marker stays under the real flap position. Checked in Chrome with HUD captures: on the runway with LAND set (marker under LAND), and at 193 km/h with LAND set (red, marker under UP). The same session also showed the biplane&#39;s flaps drooping from the lower wing (first visual check of the flap surfaces; turboprop and jet still not seen). tsc OK." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_8tj5iymd</bpmn:incoming>
